<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil firm, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil firm, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained firm on good demand from processing plants in central Indian markets. Prices were up by 100-150 rupees per tonne. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices also remained firm on good demand in local market. Soyoil solvent was up by 200 rupees and soyoil refined was up by 100 rupees per tonne. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady. Soymeal yellow was $274-276 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west Indian ports. Rapeseed extraction was $103-105 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,400-3,450 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
